{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; d=json.load(open(\\\"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issues_index.json\\\")); nums={2016,257,2147,2584,275}; [print(json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)) for x in d if x.get(\\\"number\\\") in nums]'\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"number\": 257,\n  \"title\": \"[Question] Most idiomatic way to mix styles in same line.\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2020-08-29T23:11:10Z\",\n  \"closed_at\": \"2020-08-30T14:09:32Z\",\n  \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n  \"body\": \"Love the library, really thankful for your work here.\\r\\n\\r\\n## What I want to do\\r\\n\\r\\nUse two different colors on the same line.\\r\\n\\r\\n## How I currently achieve this\\r\\n\\r\\n[Following the documentation on styles](https://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/style.html#style-themes) I use the markup api to achieve different colors, and it works great!\\r\\n\\r\\n```python\\r\\nfrom rich.console import Console\\r\\nfrom rich.theme import Theme\\r\\ncustom_theme = Theme({\\r\\n    \\\"red\\\": \\\"#FF0000\\\",\\r\\n    \\\"green\\\": \\\"#00FF00\\\"\\r\\n})\\r\\nconsole = Console(theme=custom_theme)\\r\\nconsole.print(\\\"[red]this is red[/red] [green]and this is green[/green]\\\")\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n## Question\\r\\n\\r\\nIs there another/better way to mix styles in the same line? Or are the markup tags the best method to achieve this?\"\n}\n{\n  \"number\": 275,\n  \"title\": \"[REQUEST] console print to string\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2020-09-09T13:38:41Z\",\n  \"closed_at\": \"2020-09-09T15:05:38Z\",\n  \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n  \"body\": \"I would like to use rich in a `__repr__` method, meaning that I have to get hold of a `str`.\\r\\n```python\\r\\nconsole.print(table)\\r\\n```\\r\\nalready prints the right thing for me; can I get that same output as a string?\"\n}\n{\n  \"number\": 2016,\n  \"title\": \"[Question] How to strip all styles and their tags using log handler?\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2022-03-02T23:38:43Z\",\n  \"closed_at\": \"2022-03-07T11:46:47Z\",\n  \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n  \"body\": \"I'm using 2 instances of `RichHandler` in my logger: one to log to sdout and another to log to a file.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor the file handler, I'd like to know if I can configure it to not just print plain text, but also to remove any style tags. I've played around and can get this to work using the `Console` directly, but not when wrapped with the handler:\\r\\n\\r\\n```python\\r\\nimport logging\\r\\n\\r\\nfrom rich.console import Console\\r\\nfrom rich.logging import RichHandler\\r\\n\\r\\nconsole = Console(color_system=None)\\r\\n\\r\\nlogger = logging.getLogger()\\r\\nlogger.setLevel(logging.DEBUG)\\r\\nlogger.addHandler(RichHandler(console=console))\\r\\n\\r\\nstring = \\\"Foo [red on white]bar[/]\\\"\\r\\nconsole.print(string) # Foo bar\\r\\nconsole.log(string) # [18:33:14] Foo bar                                         log.py:13\\r\\n# Should match the two above but doesn't\\r\\nlogger.info(string) # [03/02/22 18:34:11] INFO     Foo [red on white]bar[/]      log.py:16\\r\\n```\"\n}\n{\n  \"number\": 2147,\n  \"title\": \"embedding Rich SVGs leaks styles\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2022-04-03T15:16:58Z\",\n  \"closed_at\": \"2022-04-20T11:04:21Z\",\n  \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n  \"body\": \"When embedding SVGs within a web page, the SVG styles \\\"leak\\\" in to the HTML. For instance the span style changes in the rest of the page.\\r\\n\\r\\nI'm not sure if there is some easy way to prevent that, but if not, perhaps we should generate a random ID for the SVG and update the styles to only use that UD.\"\n}\n{\n  \"number\": 2584,\n  \"title\": \"Link format string in docs to Python string formatting mini-language\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2022-10-15T15:19:24Z\",\n  \"closed_at\": \"2023-01-18T15:07:05Z\",\n  \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n  \"body\": \"In the code we see\\r\\n\\r\\n text_format: str = \\\"[progress.percentage]{task.percentage:>3.0f}%\\\",\\r\\n\\r\\nI would like this to be better documented or an hyperlink to where I could learn how to use that :>3.0f, I am looking for example to ensure the TextColumn text is always a fixed number of char, like 40, with an ellipsis, if it exceed, I was going to do it in Python before passing it to add_task, but I would like that pass the whole string to add_task instead and have it adjust the text output based on the \\\"progress\\\"  TextColumn format.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
